# A female friend, especially a woman's.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1971|author=Frank A. Petroni; Ernest A. Hirsch|title=Two, four, six, eight, when you gonna integrate?|page=192
|passage=VELMA: My best '''girl friend''' is a Mexican girl. Every time I go up on the second floor where the Negroes hang out and I'm with this girl, they're always saying things like, "Hey girl, you're out of your place with her." Well, I don't listen to them at all.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1980|author=Andre Dubus|title=Finding a Girl in America|page=157|passage=He is not deeply worried about dope, because he trusts Sharon, knows she is sensible; that she tried cigarettes with her '''girl friends''' because at thirteen she wouldn't think of death {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Beatrice Labissiere|title=The Evil Land: Nehemiah|passage=Then, the lady explained that her husband often talked to his '''girl friend''' about her.}}
# {{alt form|en|girlfriend}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1958|author=DC Comics|title=Superman's '''Girl Friend''' Lois Lane}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=The Rosen Publishing Group|title=Guys: Being Best Friends|passage=You may talk about different things with your '''girl friend''' than you do with your guy friends.}}

====Usage notes====
* The spelling of '''girl friend''' as two words is used to distinguish this term from '''[[girlfriend]]''', a girl or woman with whom one has a romantic relationship.

